  "readmeFile": "ReadmeNuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fields: FileField has a new AllowedExtensions setting (\"pdf, jpg, png\"; empty = no restriction). It is applied as the accept attribute of the file input and checked when a file arrives through the upload button, drag and drop or the script method SetFile (a rejected file shows the message on the field; from a script it throws). The list page bulk upload accepts the file types the module can read (the extension of the module's bulk file format field, otherwise xlsx / xlsm; the legacy xls / xlsb formats are not readable by the Excel library) and rejects other files with a message. The helpers FileExtensionFilter (Utils) and BulkFileTransferExtensions (DesignLogic) are public so field libraries and ProCode can apply the same rules.\nSearch layouts: the input restrictions of TextField (MaxLength) and NumberField (Min / Max / Step / MaxFractionDigits) now also apply to the search inputs of the search layout; an out-of-range or too long search value shows the same message as the detail input (the search itself is not blocked).\nSearch layouts: a link-through SelectField (for example Building.Area.Prefecture, a master reference of a linked module) placed in a search layout now loads its candidates. Link fields are read-only in detail and list layouts only; in a search layout they are condition inputs.\nList pages: the internal list-page module is now created per page frame (its name carries the page frame name), so a module that is listed in several page frames with different ListPageDesign settings (search layout name, list layout name, sort, bulk buttons and so on) shows the settings of the frame that is actually open, also when navigating between frames without reloading.\nDetail pages: a navigation that changes only the query string of the current URL (the page number or search condition that a SearchField writes to the URL, including page changes of a list with IsInMemoryPaging) no longer runs OnLocationChanging of the detail layout (nor OnLocationChangingAsync of the code-behind). The module stays on the page, so there is nothing to confirm; the handler stays registered for the real leave.\nScripts: value fields have a new method SetInitialValue(value). It applies the value like Value = value (field adjustments, link lookups and OnDataChanged included) but the field is not marked as modified, so it is not part of the submit. Use it for derived initial values on loaded records; on a new record use Value = as before, because a value that is not modified is not inserted.",
